{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73X61JqmhSy8FmJLoHP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest React is **19.3.1**. That's the `latest` tag on npm, which I checked directly today. It's newer than the 19.2 that react.dev's versions page listed in my search, so that page is out of date.\n\n- **19.2** came out October 1, 2025. It added `Activity`, React Performance Tracks, and `useEffectEvent`.\n- **19.3** is now stable. I didn't look up its release notes, so I can't say what it added.\n- **Canary builds** are on 19.3.0-canary, and the newest was published October 15, 2026.\n- **Security:** the React Server Components vulnerability was fixed in 19.0.1, 19.1.2, and 19.2.1. Any version at or above those is covered, and 19.3.1 is.\n\nTo upgrade, run `npm install react@latest react-dom@latest`.\n\nSources:\n- [React Versions](https://zh-hant.react.dev/versions)\n- [React Blog](https://react.dev/blog)\n- [npm registry: react](https://registry.npmjs.org/react)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":19374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":530},"output_tokens":344,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8afadffb-e27a-49e4-88ac-027a0ee49e8d","uuid":"5c38e0fd-f079-4e43-9d4c-09d3c0f4d322","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:46:31.446Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73X5nRH8n6NEpCpTsWD"}
